==  Python

<!--
[![PyPI](https://img.shields.io/pypi/v/sqlite-tg.svg?color=blue&logo=python&logoColor=white)](https://pypi.org/project/sqlite-tg/)
-->

Install the official `sqlite-tg` PyPi package:

```bash
pip install sqlite-tg
```

Once installed, use in your Python code like so:

```python
import sqlite3
import sqlite_tg

db = sqlite3.connect(":memory:")
db.enable_load_extension(True)
sqlite_tg.load(db)
db.enable_load_extension(False)

tg_version, = db.execute("select tg_version()").fetchone()
print(f"tg_version={tg_version}")
```

See the official [`sqlite-tg` PyPi package](https://pypi.org/project/sqlite-tg/) for more details.


==  JavaScript 

Install the official `sqlite-tg` package:

```bash
npm install sqlite-tg
```

Once installed, use in your Node.js code like so, with the [`better-sqlite3`]() library:

```js
import * as sqliteVec from "sqlite-vec";
import Database from "better-sqlite3";

const db = new Database(":memory:");
sqliteVec.load(db);

const { vec_version } = db
  .prepare("select vec_version() as vec_version;")
  .get();

console.log(`vec_version=${vec_version}`);
```

